oc describe storagecluster ocs-storagecluster -n openshift-storage

oc get cephcluster -n openshift-storage -o yaml

oc describe localvolumeset local-volume -n openshift-local-storage

Most importantly, inspect what disks the Local Storage Operator discovered:

oc get localvolumediscoveryresult discovery-result-master1.vt.ss.samsung.local \
-n openshift-local-storage -o yaml

Do the same for master2 and master3.

Also check the Rook operator logs

Run:

oc logs -n openshift-storage deploy/rook-ceph-operator | grep -Ei "osd|device|error|fail"

or, to capture more context:

oc logs -n openshift-storage deploy/rook-ceph-operator --tail=300

Likely causes

From your previous ODF setup work, the most likely reasons are:

1. The discovered disks are not marked as available (they may still have partitions, LVM, or old Ceph metadata).


2. The LocalVolumeSet is not matching any devices.


3. The StorageCluster cannot provision OSDs because no eligible local PVs exist.



Once you provide the outputs of:

oc describe storagecluster ocs-storagecluster -n openshift-storage

oc describe localvolumeset local-volume -n openshift-local-storage

oc get localvolumediscoveryresult ... -o yaml (at least one node)


we can identify exactly why OSD creation is being blocked.
